# SVG Icon in Input Field

Here's how to add a clickable search icon inside an input field:

## HTML Structure

```html
<div class="input-wrapper">
  <input type="text" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search..." />
  <svg 
    class="search-icon" 
    onclick="handleSearch()"
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" 
    viewBox="0 0 24 24" 
    fill="none" 
    stroke="currentColor" 
    stroke-width="2"
  >
    <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"></circle>
    <path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35"></path>
  </svg>
</div>
```

## CSS Styling

```css
.input-wrapper {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-block;
  width: 300px; /* Adjust as needed */
}

.input-wrapper input {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 10px 40px 10px 10px; /* Right padding for icon space */
  font-size: 16px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 4px;
}

.search-icon {
  position: absolute;
  right: 10px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  width: 20px;
  height: 20px;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: #666;
  transition: color 0.3s;
}

.search-icon:hover {
  color: #333;
}
```

## JavaScript Function

```javascript
function handleSearch() {
  const input = document.getElementById('searchInput');
  const value = input.value;

  if (value.trim() !== '') {
    console.log('Searching for:', value);
    // Your search logic here
  } else {
    alert('Please enter something to search');
  }
}
```

## Alternative: Using Button Element

For better accessibility, you can wrap the SVG in a button:

```html
<div class="input-wrapper">
  <input type="text" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search..." />
  <button type="button" class="search-button" onclick="handleSearch()">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
      <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"></circle>
      <path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35"></path>
    </svg>
  </button>
</div>
```

```css
.search-button {
  position: absolute;
  right: 5px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  background: none;
  border: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  padding: 5px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
}

.search-button svg {
  width: 20px;
  height: 20px;
  color: #666;
}

.search-button:hover svg {
  color: #333;
}
```

The button approach is better for accessibility and keyboard navigation!

